{
  "@context": "../../context.jsonld",
  "@type": "Process",
  "critical": false,
  "description": "Design pedagogy for sensor signal-conditioning circuits that convert a physical quantity (magnetic field, temperature, strain, light, liquid level) into a clean analog voltage or current ready for an ADC. Covers Hall-effect interfaces, reed-switch debounce, NTC thermistor voltage dividers with the beta model, RTD and strain-gauge Wheatstone bridges, light-sensor dividers, conductive and capacitive level sensing, and the conditioning staples (amplification, filtering, linearization, offset null, and the 4-20 mA industrial current loop). Builds on comparator, op-amp, and analog-switch devices from semiconductor-devices and precision resistors/capacitors from passive-components.",
  "early_win": false,
